NAME
====

**pkg which** - display which package installed a specific file

SYNOPSIS
========

**pkg which** [**-gopqm**] _file_
**pkg which** [**--glob**] [**--origin**] [**--path-search**] [**--quiet**]
         [**--show-match**] _file_

DESCRIPTION
===========

**pkg which** is used for displaying the package that installed _file_.

OPTIONS
=======

The following options are supported by **pkg which**:

- **-g**, **--glob**:
  Treat _file_ as a glob pattern.

- **-m**, **--show-match**:
  Show files that matched the glob pattern (requires **--glob**).

- **-o**, **--origin**:
  Show the origin of the package instead of name-version.

- **-p**, **--path-search**:
  Search for the filename in `PATH`.

- **-q**, **--quiet**:
  Be quiet.

ENVIRONMENT
===========

The following environment variables affect the execution of **pkg which**. See
`pkg.conf(5)` for further description.

- `PKG_DBDIR`

- `PATH`

FILES
=====

See `pkg.conf(5)`.

SEE ALSO
========

